  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 121 AM EST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nMonday will be a transition day across South FL with dry conditions \nand plenty of sunshine. Then the next shortwave will exit from the \nSW US towards the Gulf on Tuesday and another front will approach \nthe region from the west. This will increase shower and thunderstorm \nchances for Tuesday and Wednesday and may linger into early \nThursday. Eventually the front will move off to the east and the \nshortwave will cross and move to our east into the Atlantic, \nbringing drier conditions for the end of the work week. \n\nTemperatures will be fairly comfortable during the upcoming work \nweek with highs generally in the upper 70s to lower 80s. Low temps \nwill be in the 60s/70s through mid week and then trending a bit \ncooler to the 50s/60s by the end of the week.",
